  "name": "Drone outrunner B 40p/36s (Energies 2026)",
  "description": "Model B of the 36-slot / 40-pole drone outrunners in Koo & Shin, Energies 19(16):3845 (2026), CC BY 4.0. Table 1: 83.2 mm stator, 54 mm hub bore, 92 mm rotor, 0.4 mm air gap, 2.2 mm magnets at Br 1.23 T (catalog N35 matches), 17 mm stack, 5 turns per tooth coil (10 conductors per slot here, since two tooth coils share each slot). Read from the paper's to-scale FEM drawing: 2.75 mm parallel teeth, 1.4 mm shoes leaving a 1.55 mm mouth, and magnets at a 0.76 pole arc. The 20PN1500 stator and S18C rotor B-H curves are digitised from its Fig. 3b. The motor is delta-connected, so the voltage measured at its terminals is the phase back-EMF; coilEM reports line voltage as if wye-connected, so compare the phase value. Measured: 8.86 V peak at 1000 rpm, and 1.56 N\u00b7m at 11.6 A peak phase current with id = 0. coilEM gives about 8.7 V peak phase back-EMF (8.9 V without its third harmonic, which a delta's terminals do not show) and about 1.50 N\u00b7m: within 4%, as close as the authors' own 2D FEM (8.89 V, 1.57 N\u00b7m). Published hardware data, not a coilEM benchmark: there is no pass/fail.",
